- Optional per-path directives can be added after the path. Use --$slam ARTIST_NAME to force an artist, --$copy DESTINATION to copy and tag that path's folders at the destination, or --$copy-delete DESTINATION to copy/move, verify when needed, delete the original, and tag the transferred folders. Legacy -$slam still works.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- The order of --$slam and the copy directive does not matter, but a single line cannot contain both --$copy and --$copy-delete. Destination folders must already exist and must be fully qualified paths.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Before inventory starts, TLO checks whether each copy destination has enough free space for the source root or roots assigned to it. If a destination is short on space, TLO stops and reports the destination, the affected source path or paths, and how much additional space is needed.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- When this capacity check is needed, the console first prints a Note explaining that TLO is checking source folder sizes before it checks destination capacity. Large roots can take a while to total, similar to opening folder Properties.}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx9288\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Volume label behavior: If no bracketed prefix is supplied, TLO uses the operating-system volume label for comparison and logging when available. Use [Volume] only when it matches the mounted drive label. Use [] only when an explicitly blank volume is intended and the mounted drive label is blank or unavailable.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
8. Running the main GUI}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Start the Windows GUI with TLOHome/apps/Windows/tlo-ggi.exe, or the WSL/Linux GUI from TLOHome/apps/Linux. The GUI can also be preloaded with command-line arguments such as --TLOHome, --search-path, --compliant, --as-is-artist-name, --etree-lookup, --setlistfm-lookup, --performance-mode, and --max-workers. The main Inventory and Search windows no longer show an editable TLOHome box; the startup value is used for the whole session.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
On native Windows installations, drag a folder from File Explorer and drop it onto the Search Path text box. The dropped folder replaces the Search Path value. If a file is dropped, TLO uses the containing folder.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
The upper-right hamburger menu includes Donate. Donate > Venmo displays @James-Scarano-3. Donate > Check displays James Scarano, 49 Majestic Ave., Nashua, NH 03063. Venmo and Check are submenu items with chevrons. Their detail rows use normal dark menu text instead of disabled gray text.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
The GUI and CLI share the same defaults through the internal option registry. setlist.fm still depends on etreeDB: command-line startup rejects --setlistfm-lookup unless --etree-lookup is also supplied, and the GUI automatically selects etreeDB when setlist.fm is selected.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
When you click Inventory, the Inventory button grays out immediately, Tag and Add Shows are disabled, and the output pane reports that the request was accepted while TLO prepares the roots. Existing labeled-volume overlap is resolved automatically from the same/parent/child/non-overlap path rules; TLO does not ask a Skip/Re-inventory question.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
If you click Quit while a full inventory scan is active, TLO immediately warns that it will take a moment to clean up before exiting, then stops active workers and removes active run logs.}
